  "$comment": "Golden vectors for the photo pick, photo/{head_id}/pick (sync.proto rule 6 PHOTO PICK). Every implementation (the TS helpers in this package, fc-coordinator's Push validation, fc-mobile) must agree with every case. `pushes`: one pushed SyncEvent each, on `key`. `op` is the SyncOp; the payload on the wire is JSON.stringify(`body`), or `raw` exactly as written when the case has one. `mediaBase` is the server's public media base, the top-level one unless the case names its own. `expect` is \"accepted\" or \"payload_invalid\", and `why` says which check refuses: \"schema\" (schemas/photo-pick.schema.json does not validate the payload, or it is not JSON), \"foreign\" (the schema validates and isPublicImageUrl(url, mediaBase) is false: the address is not on this server's media base) or \"delete_payload\" (a DELETE carries a payload). A DELETE with an empty payload is accepted and means \"use the default\". `lastWriterWins`: the events of one user on one figure's pick; a reader applies an event iff its version is greater than the one it holds (compareVersion), so in EVERY arrival order, repeats included, the pick ends as `expect`: the url, or null for the default.",
